        "original_id": "c625d610-17ba-5ba0-9e25-05d2f6478d9b",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: BWI Rail Station, Washington, D.C., Boston, Baltimore, Philadelphia, New York City\n- Companies: Amtrak\n- Services: Acela Express, Northeast Regional, Vermonter, Palmetto, MARC Penn Line\n- Systems: Northeast Corridor\n\nFacts:\n- BWI Rail Station is served by Amtrak intercity services, including frequent Northeast Regional and Acela Express trains and the daily Vermonter and Palmetto.\n- BWI Rail Station is also served by MARC Penn Line regional rail service.\n- Acela Express, colloquially abbreviated to Acela, is Amtrak's flagship service on the Northeast Corridor in the northeastern United States.\n- Acela Express operates between Washington, D.C. and Boston with 14 intermediate stops, including Baltimore, Philadelphia, and New York City.",
